# CLAUDE.md — Engreitz Lab Living Repository

This repository is a **mycelium-enabled living repository**, customized with the
**Engreitz Lab** convention pack. It carries its own memory (`.living/`) and
registers every analysis into the lab-wide `EngreitzLabVault`.

## Quick Orientation

1. **Read `.living/INDEX.md` first** — the auto-regenerated knowledge map (tag
   clusters, recent entries). The SessionStart hook refreshes it each session.
2. **Targeted lookup:** run `recall_lessons.py` (see mycelium core) with `--tag`,
   `--id`, or `--since`.
3. **Read `ENVIRONMENTS_INSTALLATIONS.md`** — this repo uses **pixi / mise+renv**,
   never uv/conda (see `.living/conventions/engreitz-lab/environment-conventions.md`).
4. **Read the relevant manifest** (`ANALYSIS_MANIFEST.md`, `DATA_MANIFEST.md`, …).

## Lab conventions (read these — they override mycelium defaults)

- **`.living/conventions/engreitz-lab/environment-conventions.md`** — pixi for
  Python/mixed, mise+renv for pure R, Sherlock/Oak storage, **no global installs**.
  Replaces mycelium's uv/conda guidance.
- **`.living/conventions/engreitz-lab/data-conventions.md`** — **raw data lives on
  Sherlock (`$GROUP_HOME`/`$SCRATCH`) or Drive; the repo holds manifests +
  paths, not bytes.** Never commit raw or sensitive data.
- **`.living/conventions/engreitz-lab/analysis-conventions.md`** — reports via
  `/engreitzlab-report` → `/analysis-report` (Quarto, Nature-style); genome
  views via `/igv`; every analysis auto-registered in the Vault.
- **`.living/conventions/engreitz-lab/figure-conventions.md`** — every figure is
  Nature-styled and saved as **both vector PDF and PNG** (use the `nature_style`
  helper); never PNG-only.

## The EngreitzLabVault

Every analysis is registered as a **lean pointer note** (question + repo/Sherlock
path + datasets/owner as `[[wikilinks]]`) in the private `EngreitzLabVault` at
launch, automatically, through the fail-closed vault-ingest gate. Skipped writes
(sensitive/high-risk) are logged to `.living/` for manual handling. The Vault is
the discovery layer across projects — the note points back to this repo; it never
duplicates data.

## Core convention packs (auto-installed)

- **engreitz-lab** — lab environment/data/analysis conventions (above).
- **robust-analysis** — defensive execution: fail loudly, assert shapes, sensitivity
  sweeps, null tests. See `.living/conventions/robust-analysis/`.
- (mycelium may also install `report-generator` / `idea-generator`; in this lab,
  prefer `/analysis-report` over `report-generator`.)

### Domain (opt-in)

No domain conventions installed yet. Install with mycelium's `install-convention`
mode (e.g., "install bioinformatics conventions").

## Data Conventions (summary — full text in the pack)

- **Raw/sensitive bytes never live in the repo.** They live on Sherlock or Drive;
  the repo stores manifest rows with `location`, `owner`, `sensitivity`, `access`.
- **Sensitive / Stanford High-Risk data → `$SCRATCH` only**, never `$GROUP_HOME`,
  never Git/GitHub.
- **Sherlock transfers via the DTN** (`engreitz@dtn.sherlock.stanford.edu`).
- **Never `chmod`/`setfacl` on Oak from Claude** — emit the command, ask the user.

## After Every Significant Action (Post-Action Hook Protocol)

Follow mycelium's post-action protocol (update manifests + docs, log
decisions/learnings/findings, run `validate_structure.py`, write
`.claude/last-session.md`). In this lab the protocol additionally registers the
analysis into the Vault (handled by the vault bridge — automatic).

